@startuml Deal Management Application - Component Diagram

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam componentBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam interfaceBackgroundColor #e8f5e9
skinparam interfaceBorderColor #4caf50
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam packageBorderColor #9e9e9e

' Title
title Deal Management Application - Component Diagram (C4 Level 3)

' Container boundary
package "REST API Container" <<Container>> {

    ' Controller Components
    component DealController <<Component: Servlet>> #e3f2fd

    ' HTTP handling interface
    interface "HttpServlet" as httpServlet <<Jakarta Servlet API>> #e8f5e9
    interface "BaseServlet" as baseServlet <<Base Class>> #e8f5e9
}

package "Business Logic Container" <<Container>> {

    ' Service Components
    component DealService <<Component: Service>> #fff3e0

    component UserService <<Component: Service>> #fff3e0
}

package "Data Access Container" <<Container>> {

    ' Repository Components
    component H2DealRepository <<Component: Repository>> #f3e5f5

    component H2UserRepository <<Component: Repository>> #f3e5f5

    component DatabaseManager <<Component: Singleton>> #f3e5f5

    ' Repository interface
    interface "Repository<T>" as repoInterface <<Interface>> #e8f5e9
}

package "Domain Model" <<Package>> {
    ' Domain model components
    component Deal <<Component: Entity>> #c8e6c9

    component DealProduct <<Component: Value Object>> #c8e6c9
    component DealStatus <<Component: Enum>> #c8e6c9
}

' Infrastructure
component JsonHelper <<Component: Utility>> #ffe0b2

database "H2 Database" as db <<Database>> #f3e5f5

' Relationships - Controller layer
DealController -up-|> baseServlet
baseServlet -up-|> httpServlet
DealController --> DealService : delegates to

' Relationships - Service layer
DealService --> repoInterface : uses
UserService --> repoInterface : uses
DealService ..> Deal : creates/validates

' Relationships - Repository layer
H2DealRepository .up.|> repoInterface : implements
H2UserRepository .up.|> repoInterface : implements
H2DealRepository --> DatabaseManager : gets connection from
H2UserRepository --> DatabaseManager : gets connection from
H2DealRepository --> db : executes SQL
H2UserRepository --> db : executes SQL
H2DealRepository ..> Deal : maps to/from

' Relationships - Domain model
Deal *--> "*" DealProduct : contains
Deal --> DealStatus : has

' Relationships - Utilities
DealController ..> JsonHelper : uses for serialization
H2DealRepository ..> JsonHelper : uses for products

' Component notes
note bottom of DealController
  <b>Presentation Layer Controller</b>

  Handles HTTP request/response:
  • doGet() - List/retrieve deals
  • doPost() - Create deals, close deal
  • doPut() - Update deals
  • doDelete() - Delete deals

  <b>Responsibilities:</b>
  • Parse HTTP requests
  • Validate request format
  • Map to HTTP status codes
  • Format JSON responses

  <b>No Business Logic!</b>
  Delegates all business operations
  to DealService.
end note

note bottom of DealService
  <b>Business Logic Layer</b>

  Core business operations:
  • createDeal() - Validates and creates
  • updateDeal() - Validates and updates
  • deleteDeal() - Enforces delete rules
  • closeDealAsWon() - Closes deal
  • getDealsByStatus() - Filters deals
  • calculatePipelineValue() - Metrics

  <b>Business Rules:</b>
  • "Deal title is required"
  • "Deal value must be positive"
  • "Can only delete OPEN deals"
  • "Can only close OPEN deals"

  <b>Validation Location:</b>
  validateDeal() private method
end note

note right of UserService
  <b>User Management Service</b>

  User operations:
  • createUser()
  • updateUser()
  • authenticate()
  • findByEmail()

  Used for:
  • Sales rep assignment
  • Authentication
  • User management
end note

note bottom of H2DealRepository
  <b>Deal Repository Implementation</b>

  JDBC-based persistence:
  • findAll() - SELECT * FROM deals
  • findById() - SELECT by ID
  • save() - INSERT or UPDATE
  • deleteById() - DELETE by ID

  <b>Key Techniques:</b>
  • PreparedStatement (SQL injection prevention)
  • ResultSet mapping (ORM concepts)
  • JSON serialization (for products list)
  • ID generation (DEAL-{UUID})

  <b>SQL Operations:</b>
  Translates method calls to SQL queries
  and maps results back to Deal objects.
end note

note right of H2UserRepository
  <b>User Repository Implementation</b>

  JDBC-based persistence:
  • findAll()
  • findById()
  • findByEmail()
  • save()
  • deleteById()

  Manages user accounts
  and authentication data.
end note

note right of DatabaseManager
  <b>Connection Management</b>

  Singleton that provides:
  • Connection pooling
  • Schema initialization
  • Connection lifecycle

  <b>Pattern:</b>
  Singleton Pattern

  <b>Thread-safe:</b>
  Synchronized getInstance()
end note

note right of repoInterface
  <b>Repository Interface</b>

  Generic contract:
  +findAll(): List<T>
  +findById(id): Optional<T>
  +save(entity: T): T
  +deleteById(id): boolean
  +generateId(): String

  <b>Purpose:</b>
  Abstracts data access,
  allows swapping implementations
  (H2 → MySQL, PostgreSQL, etc.)
end note

note bottom of Deal
  <b>Deal Entity</b>

  Domain object representing a sales deal:
  • id, title, status
  • salesRepId
  • products (List<DealProduct>)
  • closeDate
  • calculateTotalValue()

  <b>Statuses:</b>
  OPEN, WON, LOST, CANCELLED
end note

note right of JsonHelper
  <b>JSON Serialization Utility</b>

  Uses Gson for:
  • toJson() - Object to JSON string
  • fromJson() - JSON string to Object

  Used by:
  • Controller (request/response)
  • Repository (products storage)
end note

note as N1
  <b>Dependency Injection Flow</b>

  Application startup creates dependencies
  in bottom-up order:

  1. DatabaseManager.getInstance()
  2. H2DealRepository(dbManager)
  3. DealService(dealRepository)
  4. DealController(dealService)

  Each layer depends on interface/abstraction
  from layer below (Dependency Inversion Principle).
end note

legend right
  <b>C4 Model - Level 3: Component Diagram</b>

  Zooms into the REST API container to show
  the key components and their interactions.

  <b>Component Definition:</b>
  A component is a grouping of related functionality
  encapsulated behind a well-defined interface.

  <b>Layered Architecture:</b>

  <b>Layer 1: Presentation (Controller)</b>
  • DealController - HTTP request/response handling
  • Extends BaseServlet for common functionality
  • No business logic, only HTTP concerns

  <b>Layer 2: Business Logic (Service)</b>
  • DealService - Business rules and validation
  • UserService - User management
  • Core business operations and rules

  <b>Layer 3: Data Access (Repository)</b>
  • H2DealRepository - Deal persistence
  • H2UserRepository - User persistence
  • Repository<T> interface for abstraction
  • DatabaseManager - Connection management

  <b>Cross-Cutting:</b>
  • JsonHelper - JSON serialization utility
  • Deal, DealProduct - Domain model

  <b>Key Patterns:</b>
  • Layered Architecture (separation of concerns)
  • Repository Pattern (data abstraction)
  • Dependency Injection (constructor-based)
  • Singleton (DatabaseManager)

  <b>Dependencies Flow Down:</b>
  Controller → Service → Repository → Database

  <b>Audience:</b>
  • Developers
  • Technical architects
  • Code reviewers
endlegend

@enduml